I think the bump of the dependency is fine (would like an ack from @logicalhan), but it introduces a breaking change we need to adjust for. The simplest thing we can do is In our SummaryOpts#toPromSummaryOpts method, we can preserve the existing behavior:

```go
if opts.Objectives == nil {
  // preserve compatibility with pre-1.0 prometheus usage
  opts.Objectives = map[float64]float64{0.5: 0.05, 0.9: 0.01, 0.99: 0.001}
}
```
